Use task.json and the four named source records. The candidate register supports only a provisional result. Apply the full condition audit, including scoped exceptions, before fixing selectedItems and measure. Apply authorization only to decision: selection evidence and permission to execute are distinct. Follow the exact tie rule and output formats. If nothing qualifies, use no_action. Do not infer facts absent from current and accumulated source records.

The four pass-*.md records are read-only evidence inputs. Preserve their complete contents exactly. Do not rewrite or paraphrase them; write only decision.json.","output_path":"decision.json","output_contract":{"format":"JSON object with exactly these 4 typed fields: caseId (string), selectedItems (string), measure (string), decision (string). No extra keys.","fields":{"caseId":"Exact request identifier for the constrained resource-window scheduling decision.","selectedItems":"Up to 2 complete item IDs joined by exactly semicolon and one space; in ranked order; none if no item qualifies.","measure":"Corresponding completion time in minutes values as digits in the selected-item order, joined by exactly semicolon and one space; none if no item qualifies. Unit: minutes.","decision":"Use assign only when the eligible selection is nonempty and an operations lead release for request SCHED-540 is recorded; otherwise use hold. Use no_action only when no item qualifies. Return one bare literal: assign, hold, no_action."},"intermediate_field_enums":{"decision":["pending","assign","hold","no_action"]},"final_field_enums":{"decision":["assign","hold","no_action"]},"carry_forward":"During note passes, Maintain a complete running evidence record in readable prose, not a Draft-shaped JSON summary. Preserve every observed candidate eligibility finding, exact metric and unit, and the exact named authority prerequisite and its observed status. When later applicable evidence supersedes earlier uncertainty or a prior current-status statement, preserve that earlier statement only as explicitly labeled earlier-pass history, then append a clearly labeled current status tied to the latest evidence. The latest applicable observed evidence controls final interpretation. Do not leave conflicting current-status statements unresolved, but do not require global prose rewriting of the accumulated history. Carry supported facts forward; keep facts absent from current evidence and prior notes unknown or pending. An outstanding or next-step note is not evidence that a fact is present in the current file. Complete only this evidence pass. Do not collapse notes into selected IDs, measures, or a decision; the final interpreter makes the decision from the accumulated record. Keep historical events distinct from the requested decision. Do not invent facts. The loop carries Neuralese<string> notes, not a Draft. The final interpreter applies exactly the explicit decisionRule to the accumulated evidence record and outputContract; it does not require proof that the requested decision was already executed or add unstated prerequisites.","enum_contract":"intermediate_field_enums constrain only the initialDraft placeholder; final_field_enums constrain only the final Draft. Neither constrains the accumulated Neuralese<string> notes. Enum fields in the final Draft must contain exactly one listed literal, with no explanation or added units.","initial_state":"initialDraft is an incomplete working placeholder; final output must satisfy all declared field formats and decision rules.","decision_rule":"A work window qualifies only when the required skill is staffed, the resource is available for the full interval, and the assignment respects the worker rest rule. Select up to two qualifying windows with the earliest completion time, ties by ascending complete window ID. Assignment requires an operations lead release. Selection cardinality: up to 2; ascending completion time in minutes; ties by ascending complete ID Decision mapping: if no item qualifies, use no_action; if the nonempty eligible selection has an operations lead release for request SCHED-540 recorded, use assign; otherwise use hold. The authority is scoped to request SCHED-540; do not add a separate item-specific authorization requirement.","evidence_files":"The four pass-*.md files are read-only evidence inputs. Preserve their complete text exactly; do not rewrite, paraphrase, or replace them. Only decision.json is a writable output."},"initialDraft":{"caseId":"UNKNOWN","selectedItems":"pending","measure":"pending","decision":"pending"},"passes":[{"name":"request scope and rule","constraint":"Copy the complete request identifier and preserve the complete decision rule, including the empty-selection and authorization branches.","allowed_fields":["caseId"],"evidence_path":"pass-01-request.md","source_scope":"request SCHED-540"},{"name":"candidate register","constraint":"Make a provisional ordering or worklist from registered metrics only. Eligibility, exceptions, and authorization have not yet been checked; keep it provisional.","allowed_fields":["selectedItems","measure"],"evidence_path":"pass-02-register.md","source_scope":"register for SCHED-540"},{"name":"conditions and exceptions","constraint":"Apply every stated condition and scoped exception to the candidates. Recompute the selected set and measure; add no unstated conditions.","allowed_fields":["selectedItems","measure"],"evidence_path":"pass-03-conditions.md","source_scope":"condition audit for SCHED-540"},{"name":"execution authority","constraint":"Keep the evidence-derived selection and measure. Determine whether this source records the exact authority prerequisite: an operations lead release for request SCHED-540. The authority is scoped to request SCHED-540; do not add a separate item-specific authorization requirement. Authority affects only the decision; an empty eligible selection remains no_action.","allowed_fields":["decision"],"evidence_path":"pass-04-authority.md","source_scope":"authority record for SCHED-540"}]}

